  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the biological pathway leading to KB through multiple indirect routes. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for various molecules, which in turn target KB. Specifically, Mollicellin N is linked to Leukocyte common antigen and A704, both of which are targets of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid, which ultimately targets KB. This indicates a hierarchical relationship where Mollicellin N serves as a starting point for a series of molecular interactions culminating in KB. The presence of multiple distinct targets (Leukocyte common antigen, A704, and LC4-1) suggests that Mollicellin N may engage in diverse molecular interactions, potentially through different pathways or mechanisms. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship between Mollicellin N and KB, emphasizing the role of 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid as a central mediator in this network.",
